      "id": "0otcgin",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Industry"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Industries are secondary economic activities that transform raw materials into finished goods of higher value.",
        "Classification of industries is based on raw materials (agro-based, mineral-based), size (micro, small, medium, large), and ownership (public, private, joint, cooperative).",
        "India has eight major industrial regions, including Mumbai-Pune, Hugli, Bengaluru-Tamil Nadu, and the mineral-rich Chota Nagpur belt.",
        "Industrial location depends on key factors like availability of raw materials, power, labor, transport, market, and supportive government policies.",
        "The 1991 Industrial Policy marked a paradigm shift towards Liberalization, Privatization, and Globalization (LPG) in the Indian economy."
      ],
      "id": "wfi2s5l"
    },
