    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Chota Nagpur region is termed the 'Ruhr of India' due to its rich concentration of iron and steel industries and mineral wealth.",
        "Mumbai was historically designated as the 'Cottonopolis of India' owing to its favorable humid climate and port facilities.",
        "The Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956 is known as the Economic Constitution of India and prioritized public sector expansion."
